From 1f2bdcbda4640483309c897b034ab77b6a494eb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:13:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm, VideoRenderers: Dolby Vision sent as HDR10+,
 as an option

A setting under System > Display, below "Dolby Vision as HDR10 when needed":
"Send it as HDR10+ where the display takes it" (videoscreen.hadesdvashdr10plus,
off by default: the display then maps the picture otherwise than plain HDR10).
Where it is on, the display declares HDR10+ and its driver has HDR10PLUS_VSIF,
and the picture is not mapped to the display, a Dolby Vision picture rebuilt
as HDR10 goes out with HDR10+ dynamic metadata measured from it
(tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_dvplus.h): profile 8.1 is rebuilt too then.

- The renderer asks the window system for the InfoFrame of each frame before
  its picture is drawn (DVConversionHDR10Plus()), and hands it to the HDR10+
  output that already sends a film's own (CWinSystemGbm::SetHDR10Plus(): the
  payload in the commit of its frame, no change of mode, the HDMI VSIF never
  touched, plain HDR10 where the driver refuses it). A frame of the window that
  shows no rebuilt picture goes out without it.
- The window system takes the samples of each rebuilt picture once it is drawn
  (DVPlusMeasure(), the film's area of its level 5 block) and reads them back
  without waiting; the scenes are those of the RPU.
- kodi.log says once a video whether it is sent and why not, the first values
  sent, every 240 frames what was sent, and a summary at the end.
- The Dolby Vision page of the player information says "Dolby Vision rebuilt,
  sent as HDR10+ (metadata measured by Hades)" while it goes out
  (hades.dv.hdr10plus); the overview page already says "HDR10+ (PQ)" and the
  values sent. Its variable for other skins is made again with
  make-playerinfo.py (system/hades/HadesIncludes.xml); the dialog it makes,
  DialogHadesPlayerInfo.xml, is stale already before this commit (the row "GPU
  by pass") and is left as it is, for a later commit to make again.
- Strings: core 40926 and 40927 (en_gb), Estuary 32100 to 32102 (en_gb, es_es,
  es_ar, es_mx).

Not seen on a display: only a TV that takes HDR10+ can say what it does with
these metadata.
